  "query_preview": "into Monday night. \n\nFor Sunday, easterly winds increase further to 30 kts with \noccasional gusts upwards of 35 kts, particularly this morning. \nSeas continue to build to 7-10 feet by Sunday afternoon. A Small\nCraft Advisory is in effect for the Delaware Bay and all of the\nAtlantic coastal waters until tonight. Due to the occasional \nnature of gale force gusts, the Gale Watch has been cancelled \nfor the offshore waters. Visibility restrictions are likely in \nrain which could be moderate to heavy at times.\n\nWinds shift more southerly and diminish below advisory criteria as\nthe low center moves across the waters overnight before shifting\nmore northerly as the low begins to depart early Monday morning.\nSeas will be slow to subside, staying elevated around 6-8 feet.\n\nOutlook...\n\nMonday...SCA conditions for the coastal ocean waters due to \nlingering seas of 6-8 feet and northerly wind gusts upwards of \n25 kts that gradually diminish into Monday night.\n\nTuesday through Thursday...No marine hazards expected.",
